---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Brand from '../components/Brand.astro';
import ContactBand from '../components/ContactBand.astro';
import Video from '../components/Video.astro';
---
<Base title="Our robots" description="Meet the compact mobile robot platform behind packsel warehouse automation. Explore transport and shelf configurations, specifications, and video.">
<section class="container page-intro"><p class="kicker">Meet the hardware</p><h1>Your warehouse.<br>A new kind of workhorse.</h1><p class="lead">A compact mobile platform, configured for the job. Explore the hardware behind <Brand tm /> warehouse automation.</p></section>
<section class="container product-feature"><div class="product-plate"><img src="/images/transport-robot.webp" width="800" height="1200" alt="packsel standard transport robot product visualization" /><span class="mono plate-caption">Product visualization · platform configuration</span></div><div class="stack"><p class="kicker">Platform transport</p><h2>Built to carry<br>the daily workload.</h2><p class="lead">A low mobile base, an onboard touchscreen, and a loading platform for point-to-point transport.</p><div class="spec-strip"><div><strong>300 kg</strong><span>Maximum payload</span></div><div><strong>1.2 m/s</strong><span>Maximum speed</span></div><div><strong>8 h</strong><span>Full-load runtime*</span></div></div><p class="note">Published standard-platform specifications. Runtime depends on the route, load, and operating conditions. Final specifications are confirmed in your proposal.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="mailto:zach@packsel.co?subject=Robot%20configuration%20enquiry">Find your configuration ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="section-large container split"><div class="stack"><p class="kicker">Shelf transport</p><h2>More organization.<br>On every trip.</h2><p class="lead">Multi-level carrying space keeps totes and materials organized. A picking configuration can pair separate order bins with a scan-guided workflow.</p><p class="secondary">Our interactive demo uses nine order bins to illustrate zone picking. The shelf arrangement and software workflow are designed around your requirements.</p><a class="text-link" href="/warehouse-demo/">See the picking concept →</a></div><figure><img class="wide-photo" src="/images/warehouse-robots.webp" width="1440" height="960" alt="Illustrative shelf configuration with totes and cartons behind the robot touchscreen" loading="lazy" /><figcaption class="note">Illustrative shelf configuration; final hardware may differ.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="surface-sunken section-large"><div class="container split"><div class="stack"><p class="kicker">Under the surface</p><h2>Know the platform.</h2><p>These are reference specifications for the standard transport configuration. Payload dimensions and accessories affect the clearance your operation needs.</p></div><div class="table-scroll"><table class="spec-table"><caption class="visually-hidden">Standard transport platform reference specifications</caption><tbody>{[['Maximum payload','300 kg / 661 lb'],['Base dimensions (L × W × H)','835 × 500 × 1,350 mm'],['Maximum travel speed','1.2 m/s'],['Runtime at full load','8 hours'],['Runtime without load','12 hours'],['Charge time, 0–90%','2 hours'],['Navigation','VSLAM + LiDAR SLAM']].map(([label,value])=><tr><th scope="row">{label}</th><td>{value}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><p class="note">Reference: supplied product specification, December 2025. Ratings are not a site-specific performance guarantee.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="container section-large split"><div class="stack"><p class="kicker">See it move</p><h2>The platform<br>in action.</h2><p class="lead">Watch the robot navigate, carry materials, and support repeat transport tasks.</p></div><Video /></section><ContactBand />
</Base>
